Rules:
  [P1] Use FastAPI for new APIs, Django for full-stack apps.
  [P2] Use Pydantic for request/response validation.
  [P3] Use SQLAlchemy 2.0+ for database access.
  [P4] Use dependency injection for service layer.
  [P5] Use Celery for background task processing.
  [P6] Use Redis for caching and session storage.
  [P7] Implement JWT authentication with proper expiry.
  [P8] Use Alembic for database migrations.

Pros:
  - Rapid development
  - Excellent documentation
  - Strong ecosystem

Cons:
  - Performance overhead
  - Async complexity in Django
  - Migration management

Alternatives:
  - Go (performance)
  - Node.js (full-stack JS)
  - Spring Boot (enterprise)

State: +

